{title: Praise the Lord! Ye Heavens, Adore Him}
{artist: Foundling Hospital Collection}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 92}

Verse 1
[F]Praise the Lord! ye [Bb]heavens, a[F]dore him; [Dm]praise him, [Bb]angels [C]in the [F]height;
sun and moon, re[Bb]joice be[F]fore him — [Dm]praise him, [Bb]all ye [C]stars of [F]light.

Verse 2
[F]Praise the Lord, for He is glorious; [Bb]Never shall His promise fail. [Dm]God hath made His [Bb]saints victorious; [C]Sin and death [F]shall not
prevail. Praise the God of our salvation; Hosts on high, His pow'r [Dm]proclaim. Heav'n and [Bb]earth and all creation, [C]Laud and magnify [F]His name.

Verse 3
[F]Worship, honor, glory, blessing, Lord, we offer [Bb]unto Thee. Young and old, [Dm]Thy praise expressing, In [Bb]glad homage [C]bend the knee. [F]All the
saints in Heav'n adore Thee; We would bow before Thy throne. As [Dm]Thine angels serve [Bb]before Thee, So on [C]earth Thy will [F]be done.
